      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Can you check when this happens whether the EAC driver is still loaded? In a command prompt, run `sc query EasyAntiCheat_EOSSys`. When you aren't running VRChat or any other EAC software, you should get either \"The specified service does not exist as an installed service.\" or \"STATE: 1 STOPPED\". It should not say \"STATE: 4 RUNNING\" or \"STATE: 3 STOP_PENDING\".\n\nI have been having a similar problem and believe the problem is related to EAC. https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/eac-failing-to-unload-preventing-starting-vrchat-again\n\nEdit: Stopped state is okay.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-10-24T15:29:35.521Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "About 50% of the time when I exit VRChat, it does not properly inform Steam of game shutdown. Steam shows VRChat as \"Running\" even though VRChat.exe has fully exited and is no longer visible in Task Manager. The \"Stop game\" button within Steam does nothing. Since Steam thinks the game is already running, it won't launch another instance of VRChat. I'm forced to restart all of Steam in order to relaunch VRChat. This is annoying and awkward when I'm in VR, and have to take off the headset to restart Steam and SteamVR via keyboard and mouse. It's even worse when I'm using Airlink to play with a Quest using full-body tracking, as I'm forced to recalibrate the Oculus and SteamVR playspaces. It's doubly aggravating when I've been crashed by a malicious user in-game; feels like salt in the wound. Most of the time when this happens now, I'll just play another game instead of restarting and recalibrating my whole setup.\nNo other game in my Steam library has this problem. The issue is unique to VRChat.",
